\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Verifiable reward}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{rlvr}
\tag{reward}

\p{Given a verifier #{V} and a declared score map
#{s:\mathcal E\times\{\mathsf{pass},\mathsf{fail}\}\to\mathbb R}, the
\strong{verifiable reward} is}

##{
  R_V(x,y)=s(V(x,y)).
}

\p{A reward is verifiable when a component that can change the update is
computed from reproducible evidence rather than an unaudited model judgment.
The score map may still combine accuracy, format, and other declared checks.}

\p{The rule rewards in \citet{Section 2.2}{guo2025deepseek} and the outcome
rewards used with GRPO in \citet{Section 4.1}{shao2024deepseekmath} are source
instances. The general definition is an FTIP synthesis across these uses.}
